# Template only. Copy to .env for local development; .env is gitignored.
#
# THIS FILE MUST NEVER CONTAIN A REAL VALUE. It is tracked, and the repo goes
# public after launch (D68) — anything committed here is permanent and public.
# Real values live in GitHub Actions secrets or host environment config, are
# never echoed, never interpolated into a log line, and never passed as a Docker
# build ARG (build args land in image history). See D60.

# local | ci | staging | production
ENVIRONMENT=local

# CRITICAL | ERROR | WARNING | INFO | DEBUG
LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# Two URLs, and they are NOT interchangeable (D62).
#
# DATABASE_URL is the POOLED Neon endpoint (the host WITH `-pooler`). The app
# runs here: many short transactions, no session state. app/db.py disables both
# prepared-statement caches and uses NullPool, because pgbouncer IS the pool.
#
# DATABASE_URL_DIRECT is the DIRECT endpoint (the host WITHOUT `-pooler`), and
# Alembic is the only thing that may use it. migrations/env.py refuses to run
# without it and will NOT fall back to the pooled one: Alembic's version lock is
# connection-scoped, and a transaction pooler does not preserve it.
#
# Both unset here, so /readyz reports "database not configured" — the honest
# state of a checkout with no database, and the state the test suite runs in.
#
# Note the `+asyncpg` in the scheme. A bare `postgresql://` selects the sync
# psycopg dialect, which is not installed, and the error names psycopg.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://user:password@ep-x-pooler.region.neon.tech/dbname
# DATABASE_URL_DIRECT=postgresql+asyncpg://user:password@ep-x.region.neon.tech/dbname
